\label{mainthmA}
$\CH_c(n)$ grows at least as fast as $n^{2}/4$. More precisely,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:liminf}
\liminf_{n\to\infty} \frac{\CH_c(n)}{n^{2}} \ge \frac{1}{4}.
\end{equation}
Furthermore, if $\CH_c(n) < \infty$ for some $n \in \mathbb{N}$, then $\CH_c(n+1) \ge 1+\CH_c(n).$

