expanded_sketch:
The post-theorem introduction highlights as the key observation for proving the main theorem the identification of centers
\[
\mathfrak{z}(V^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1}))\simeq \mathfrak{z}(\mathcal{W}^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1}))
\]
given by the following result.

\begin{theorem}\label{them: Detecting the FF center}\hspace{0mm}\\
\textup{(1)} The homomorphism $\iota$ is an isomorphism
\begin{align*}
\iota\colon \cent(V^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1}))\xrightarrow{\simeq} \cent(\W^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1})).
\end{align*}
\textup{(2)} There is an isomorphism of differential algebras 
\begin{align*}
 \gr\cent(V^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1}))\simeq \Lambda^{n|1}_{\aff}.
\end{align*}
\end{theorem}

It then indicates that one studies the Heisenberg coset
\[
C^\kappa(\gl_{n|1})=\operatorname{Com}(\pi_J,\mathcal{W}^\kappa(\gl_{n|1}))
\]
and uses that the center \(\mathfrak{z}(\mathcal{W}^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1}))\) can be “deformed” to other levels as the specialization of this coset at the critical level, via the following statement.

\begin{theorem}\label{thm: Wakimoto for sCoset}\hspace{0mm}\\
\textup{(1) (\cite{CGN21})}
For $k \neq -\dC+1$, the embedding $\rho$ induces the embedding
\begin{align*}
    \Psi\colon C^\kk(\gl_{n|1}) \hookrightarrow  \pi^{k+\dC}_{\tori}
\end{align*}
which depends continuously on $\kk$ so that the generic image is characterized as the joint kernel of the screening operators
\begin{align*}
    C^\kk(\gl_{n|1}) \overset{\Psi}{\simeq} \bigcap_{i=1}^n \Ker S_i \subset \pi^{k+\dC}_{\tori}.
\end{align*} 
\textup{(2)} For the critical level $\kk=\kk_c$, i.e., $k=-\dC$, 
\begin{align*}
    C^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1})= \cent(\W^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1})).
\end{align*}
\end{theorem}

The outline further specifies the proof route: determine strong generators of \(\mathcal{W}^\kappa(\gl_{n|1})\) (via Feigin--Semikhatov duality), describe the center of \(\mathcal{W}^\kappa(\gl_{n|1})\) at \(\kappa=\kk_c\), then use the Wakimoto realization to relate the centers of \(\mathcal{W}^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1})\) and \(V^{\kk_c}(\gl_{n|1})\); on this basis, prove the main theorem next, first establishing it in Sections~\ref{sec: Center of affine at the critical level} and~\ref{sec: Character formula}.

