\label{main}
There exists $\varepsilon>0$ and a set $A\subset \mathbb N$ such that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For all sufficiently large $m$, $r_A(m)>\varepsilon\log m$,
\item $A$ contains no minimal additive subbasis of order $2$.
\end{enumerate}

