\begin{lemma} \label{Local}
    Let $\Omega \subset \mathbb{R}^N$ with $N=2,3$ be a bounded domain with smooth boundary. Suppose that $\kappa=0$ when $N=3$ and $\kappa=1$ when $N=2$ and \eqref{S} and \eqref{phi} hold. Then there exists a maximal existence time $T_{\rm max}\in (0, \infty]$ and a unique quadruple $(n,c,u,P)$ of functions 
