\section{Global boundedness}\label{global boundedness}
In this section, we are devoted to proving Theorem~\ref{thm1_2} by applying the method in \cite{2022-IUMJ-Winkler}. Using the well-known $W^{1,p}$ regularity theory \cite{1973-JMSJ-BrezisStrauss} to the second equation in (\ref{eq1.1.0}), we derive the following lemma.
\begin{lem}\label{nablav}
For all $k\in [1,\frac{n}{n-1})$ with $n \geq 2$, there exists a constant $C=C(k)>0$ such that
\begin{align*}
\|\nabla v(\cdot,t)\|_{L^{ k}(\Omega)} \leq C\|w(\cdot,t)\|_{L^1(\Omega)}, \quad t\in(0,T_{\max}).
