Concerning the proof (of the main theorem), the authors “argue as in \cite{b1} (see also \cite{S}) via known blow-up arguments” (\cite{bt}, \cite{det}, \cite{ls}, \cite{llty}), and they “carefully handle the various possibilities arising due to the perturbation (i.e. $\epsilon_n\rightarrow 0^+$) of the homogeneous conical singularity.” The proof is by “contradiction” and, “in each one of the blow up scenarios at hand,” it is required “to find at least one bubble coming with some large enough amount of mass.” For this reason they first prove a preliminary “minimal mass” lemma for solutions of
\begin{equation}\label{intro:eq}
 -\D v_n=\left({\epsilon_n^2+|x|^2}\right)^{\alpha_n}V_n(x)e^{\displaystyle v_n} \qquad\text{in} \,\,\, \Omega,
\end{equation}
and then prove the ``$\sup+C\inf$'' inequality later.

