ref_dict.thm:open_map:
\begin{theorem}[Invariance of domain]\label{thm:open_map}
	Let $\mathcal M=(M,<,+,0,\ldots)$ be a definably complete locally o-minimal expansion of an ordered group.
	Let $V$ be a definable open subset of $M^n$ and $f:V \to M^n$ be a definable continuous injective map.
	Then $f$ is an open map; that is, $f(U)$ is open whenever $U$ is an open subset of $V$.
\end{theorem}

