\label{thm:main}
There exists an algorithm with the following properties. 
It takes as input integers $N \geqslant 3$ and $D \geqslant 1$ with $D < N-1$.
It outputs either some $\alpha\in\Z_N^*$ with $\ord_N(\alpha) > D$
or a nontrivial divisor of $N$.
Its time complexity is
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:main-complexity}
O\left(\frac{D^{1/2}}{(\log \log D)^{1/2}} \log^2 N\right).
\end{equation}

