\begin{equation*}
\mathcal L:= \left\{(X,Y)\in \mathbb{R}^{m\times k}\times \mathbb{R}^{n \times k}:\ 
XY^{\top} = L\ \text{and}\ \mathrm{rank}(X) = \mathrm{rank}(Y) = r\right\}.
\end{equation*}
When $k=r$, the rank condition is redundant and $\mathcal L=\{(X,Y):XY^\top=L\}$.
