\begin{theorem}\label{coarseBCC}
    Let $(\Gamma, \Lambda)$ be a Hecke pair of discrete groups. If both $\Lambda$ and $X$ admit coarse embeddings into Hilbert space, then $\Gamma$ satisfies the coarse Baum--Connes conjecture and consequently the Novikov conjecture. \qed
