p-q+2<\Big(\frac{2}{n}(p-q+2)+p-q+1\Big)\big(k_1+\frac{2}{n}\big)-\frac{2}{n}(p-q+2)-p.
\end{align*}
Combining this with (\ref{k2-1}) guarantees the existence of $k_2$.

