mcq.question:
Let \(\mathbf V\) be a pseudovariety of semigroups (that is, a class of finite semigroups closed under finite direct products, subsemigroups, and homomorphic images). For a finite semigroup \(S\in\mathbf V\), let \(N=|S|\). Here, a straight-line program means a multiplication-only program over a generating set, and \("affords efficient compression"\) means that elements generated in members of \(\mathbf V\) admit such programs of polylogarithmic length in \(N\). Consider the following properties of \(\mathbf V\):
(i) \(\mathbf V\) affords efficient compression;
(ii) \(\mathbf V\) contains none of the three specific pseudovarieties \(\mathbf{LRB}\), \(\mathbf{RRB}\), and \(\mathbf T\);
(iii) \(\mathbf V\) admits straight-line programs of length \(\mathcal O((\log N)^2)\).
In addition, if every group belonging to \(\mathbf V\) is solvable, also consider:
(iv) \(\mathbf V\) admits straight-line programs of length \(\mathcal O(\log N)\);
(v) \(\mathbf V\) admits straight-line programs of width \(\mathcal O(1)\) and length \(\mathcal O(\operatorname{polylog} N)\).
Which statement about these properties is valid?

