 Suppose $w_{\theta}\geq0$ in $\Sigma_{\theta}$ for some $\theta\in(0,\frac{\pi}{2})$, then there exists some $\overline{\epsilon}>0$ (depending on $\theta$), such that $\forall \epsilon\in(0,\overline{\epsilon})$, we have
\[
w_{\theta+\epsilon}(x)\geq0, \quad \forall x\in \Sigma_{\theta+\epsilon}. 
\]
\end{lemma}
