To the best of the author's knowledge, it is unknown whether the boundaries of these corks are strong.  In this paper, we address this question for specific families of corks. The families of strong corks constructed in this paper are derived from the Akbulut cork; the first member of each family is given by the boundary of the Akbulut cork.

\subsection{Main results}

First, we construct an infinite family of strong corks that generalizes the aforementioned examples of corks \((C_n,\tau)\) and \((C(m),\tau)\):

