\label{thm:main}
    Let $\rho(x,t)$ be the global-in-time solution to an unstable initial datum $\rho_0 \not\equiv \rho_s$, where 
    $$
    \rho_s(x_2) = \begin{cases}
        1, & x_2 > 0,\\
        -1, & x_2 < 0,
    \end{cases}
    $$
    is the unstable stratified state. Moreover, suppose that $\Gamma_0$ is centrally symmetric and evenly symmetric with respect to $x_1 = \pm\frac{\pi}{2}$. Then for any $\epsilon > 0$, we have
    \begin{equation}
        \label{est:main}
        \limsup_{t \to \infty} t^{-{\frac{1}{17}} + \epsilon} (L(t) + \mathcal{K}(t))= \infty.
    \end{equation}

