Under Convention \ref{conv of Determinantal rings}, we assume that $B$ is a reduced Cohen--Macaulay ring with canonical module $\w_B$.
Then $R_B(X; \d)$ is CTR if and only if $B$ is CTR and $\l-\l'\le 1$.
In these situations, let $I=\{i\mid 1\le i\le t, \l_i\ne \l_{i-1}\}$.
Then the canonical trace of $R_B(X; \d)$ is $$\Bigl(\bigcap_{i\in I} I_B(x; \tau_i)\Bigr) \cap (\tr_B (\w_B)R_B(X; \d)).$$
\end{thm}

