ref_dict.xxthm2.6:
\begin{theorem}
\label{xxthm2.6}
Let $\Lambda =\lambda M$ for some $\lambda \in \Bbbk^{\times}$ and a skew-symmetric matrix $M=(m_{ij})\in M_{n}(\mathbb{Z})$ with integer entries such that $L_{\Lambda}(\Bbbk)$ is a simple Poisson torus. Then each Poisson endomorphism of $L_{\Lambda}(\Bbbk)$ is an automorphism. That is, such a simple Poisson torus $L_{\Lambda}(\Bbbk)$ is Dixmier and thus $R$-Dixmier for any connected graded Poisson firm domain $R$. 
\end{theorem}

