    We work in the localized ring $K_0(\Stck_k)[\Lb^{-1}]$.  Localization is used to place the argument in a ring where quotient stack identities for linear algebraic groups (e.g.\ $\GL_n$, $\PGL_2$) and the power--structure identities for symmetric powers hold uniformly as equalities of rational functions, thereby justifying the reorganization of unordered local factors into Euler factors.
