\begin{theorem}[$100\%$ Characterization of $A$]\label{thm:100-percent}
Let $A \subseteq \F_p$ be a set of size $|A| = \alpha p$ with $\alpha \gg 1$, 
and let tuple $(r_1, \ldots, r_k)$ be coprime and bounded such that
\[
 |A^{r_1} + \cdots + A^{r_k}|
 \le K p^{\frac{k-1}{k}}|A|^{1/k}.
\]
Then there exist sets $P_1, \ldots, P_k \subseteq \F_p$ such that, 
after removing $O(1/\alpha)$ elements from~$A$, the following holds:
\begin{itemize}[itemsep=0.5em]
 \item $A \subseteq \sqrt[r_1]{P_1} \cap \cdots \cap \sqrt[r_k]{P_k}$;
