\begin{corollary}
\label{cor:cic-for-coefficients}
Let $u \leq v \in W$ and $u' \leq v' \in W'$ be such that $[u,v] \cong [u',v']$. Then $[q]P_{u,v}=[q]P_{u',v'}$, $[q]R_{u,v}=[q]R_{u',v'}$, $[q^{\ell(u,v)-1}]R_{u,v}=[q^{\ell(u',v')-1}]R_{u',v'}$, and $[q^{\ell(u,v)}-2]\tR_{u,v}=[q^{\ell(u',v')}-2]\tR_{u',v'}$.
\end{corollary}

Although $P_{u,v}$ can have a quadratic term when $5 \leq \ell(u,v)\leq 6$, we are nevertheless able to prove \Cref{conj:cic} for such intervals.

